# Sourced, not run. The notarytool options naming the credentials every call to the notary
# service uses: the keychain profile NOTARY_PROFILE names, found in the keychain file
# NOTARY_KEYCHAIN names, or where notarytool looks by default when NOTARY_KEYCHAIN is unset.
# A Mac's profile lives in its own keychain; the release workflow's lives in a keychain file
# it makes for the run, which notarytool reads only when told its path.
#
# [LAW:single-enforcer] scripts/release asks the profile to answer and scripts/notarize submits
# under it, so both read these options here rather than each spelling them.
profile=${NOTARY_PROFILE:?NOTARY_PROFILE names the notarytool keychain profile; make one with xcrun notarytool store-credentials}
notary_credentials=(--keychain-profile "$profile" ${NOTARY_KEYCHAIN:+--keychain "$NOTARY_KEYCHAIN"})
